diff --git a/src/open_qwen36/README.md b/src/open_qwen36/README.md
index 121f1c7..b0d047d 100644
--- a/src/open_qwen36/README.md
+++ b/src/open_qwen36/README.md
@@ -635,3 +635,23 @@ OpenAI-style chat completions:
 The same prompt twice in one server session gives the same answer (state reset
 through the app's checkpoint/restore path). Prompt cache, sampler, chat
 template, tool parsing — all the app's, unchanged.
+
+
+### Issue 212: dense prefill and container compatibility
+
+Llama's full-rotary dense prefill now uses the NPU block-attention products with
+its scaled RoPE frequencies. Both queries and softmax probabilities retain a
+BF16 high part and remainder; dropping the probability remainder failed the
+longer-prompt accuracy check. Contiguous prefill weights share the immutable
+decode pool through XRT views. The load log separates shared weight bytes from
+new allocations and the fixed-capacity KV reservation.
+
+The default export includes Llama 3.2 1B/3B and Qwen3 0.6B. Q4NX embedding lookup
+accepts both BF16 rows and native Q8 tiles; layer-major and L-row paths use the
+same lookup. This removes the upstream Qwen 27B Q8 embedding restriction, but a
+complete upstream-model run is still a separate integration check.
+
+See [the issue 212 validation report](../../specs/open-engine/issue-212-validation.md)
+for measured performance, accuracy results (including near-tie failures), exact
+inputs, build commands and remaining work. Decode context scaling and paged KV
+are not solved by these prefill/allocation changes.
